verification.refinedFix:
The bpf_loop callback ctx must point to stack, not a map value. Wrap the map pointer in a stack struct and pass its address. The `if (!s) return 0;` guard at line 161 already exists, so only the struct wrap is needed:

  struct cb_ctx { __u64 *s; };
  static int cb(__u32 i, void *ctx) {
      struct cb_ctx *c = ctx;
      *c->s += i;
      return 0;
  }
  ...
  __u64 *s = get_sum();
  if (!s) return 0;
  struct cb_ctx c = { .s = s };
  bpf_loop(10000, cb, &c, 0);

Equivalent alternative that avoids spilling a pointer across the callback boundary: accumulate into a stack scalar, then commit once after the loop:

  static int cb(__u32 i, void *ctx) { *(__u64 *)ctx += i; return 0; }
  ...
  __u64 *s = get_sum(); if (!s) return 0;
  __u64 acc = 0;
  bpf_loop(10000, cb, &acc, 0);
  *s += acc;

Either loads cleanly on 7.0.

